    {
      "id": "fact:f003",
      "label": "f003",
      "classes": "ai_fact",
      "type": "ai_fact",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-06T17:29:52.708Z",
      "concluded": "2026-09-25T02:03:05Z",
      "info": "AI-infrastructure surface (mcp-oauth / wp-abilities / MCP) investigated and confirmed hardened; no unauthenticated token issuance or ability execution found. Key confirmed facts: (1) The OAuth server is wp-media/mcp-oauth (cloned to /tmp/mcp-oauth), embedded in the site; /.well-known/oauth-authorization-server discloses issuer https://animeape.com, authorization_endpoint /oauth/authorize, token_endpoint /oauth/token, revocation_endpoint /oauth/revoke, scopes ['mcp'], code_challenge S256, grant_types [authorization_code,refresh_token], token_endpoint_auth_methods ['none'], client_id_metadata_document_supported=true. No registration_endpoint (dynamic client registration absent; /oauth/register = 404). (2) Live behavior: /oauth/authorize without client_id -> 400 'client_id is required.'; with an arbitrary client_id -> 400 'Unknown OAuth client.'. Using the bundled trusted publisher client_id https://claude.ai/oauth/mcp-oauth-client-metadata -> server successfully resolved it via CIMD and returned 400 'redirect_uri does not match registered value.', proving untrusted/any CIMD client_ids ARE dereferenced (default wpmedia_mcp_oauth_allow_untrusted_providers=true) and the flow reaches redirect_uri validation pre-login. (3) The full token path is closed: /oauth/authorize-callback and /oauth/consent both require is_user_logged_in(); auth codes are 256-bit single-use transients created only after login+nonce-gated consent; TokenEndpoint binds user_id/app_password to that logged-in user. (4) MCP transport: both /wp-json/mcp/mcp-oauth-server and /wp-json/mcp/mcp-adapter-default-server return 401 with WWW-Authenticate Bearer realm=https://animeape.com, resource_metadata=/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource (resource=https://animeape.com/wp-json/mcp/mcp-oauth-server). OAuthHttpTransport requires an HS256 JWT signed with the site 256-bit random option 'mcp_jwt_secret' (SecretManager, bin2hex(random_bytes(32))), matching aud=get_rest_url(null,'mcp/mcp-oauth-server') and iss=home_url(), with a valid sub (WP user id) and app_pass_id anchored to a live Application Password. Secret is not recoverable (no leak found); JWT is not forgeable (alg pinned to HS256, no 'none'). (5) Abilities API oracle works: wp-abilities/v1/abilities/{name}/run with the ability name using a LITERAL slash (URL-encoded %2F returns rest_no_route). Non-existent ability -> 404 code rest_ability_not_found; existing show_in_rest ability -> 401 rest_ability_cannot_execute (or 405 rest_ability_invalid_method for wrong HTTP verb, which leaks annotation type: woocommerce/product-create|update require POST, product-delete requires DELETE). Confirmed existing but permission-gated (all 401 unauth) abilities: core/get-site-info, core/get-environment-info, core/get-user-info (show_in_rest=false), woocommerce/products-query, woocommerce/product-create, woocommerce/product-update, woocommerce/product-delete, woocommerce/orders-query, woocommerce/order-update-status, woocommerce/order-add-note. The mcp-adapter/* abilities (discover-abilities, get-ability-info, execute-ability) are NOT registered on the site (404). No ability with a permissive permission_callback was found; core abilities require manage_options, WooCommerce abilities require their own caps, mcp-adapter execute-ability requires is_user_logged_in + current_user_can('read'). (6) GET /wp-json/wp-abilities/v1/abilities and /categories both return 401 rest_forbidden (list requires auth) - abilities cannot be enumerated anonymously beyond name guessing. (7) Conclusion: the MCP/Abilities/OAuth surface offers no unauthenticated RCE without first obtaining a WordPress user session; the only remaining route through it is login/registration (site /wp-login.php is Cloudflare-403 per f001). (8) Side observations while probing (outside this intent, likely more promising, feed into i003): POST /wp-json/elementor-one/v1/plugins/{slug}/activate validates slug against a whitelist (angie, manage, elementor, elementor-pro, site-mailer, image-optimization, ...) returning 400 rest_invalid_param BEFORE any auth check, so a valid slug may reach the activation handler unauthenticated (needs testing); elementor-one/v1/connect/authorize=401; themes/activate=403; reycore/v1/action POST requires param 'action' (400 rest_missing_callback_param) and is unauthenticated up to that point; gsf/v1/update-options POST returns 200 {\"error\":1,\"message\":\"shop secret Mismatch Unauthorized request\"} (secret-gated, possible bypass target); objectcache/v1/options and DELETE objectcache/v1/commands = 401. Plugin source references cloned locally: /tmp/mcp-oauth, /tmp/mcp-adapter, /tmp/abilities-api. No files saved under /home/kali/workspace/animeape except WP REST route dump wpjson_root.json.",
