      "info": "Version-fingerprint gap closed for the remaining plugins via staggered readme.txt reads (Cloudflare serves plugin readme.txt without challenge; ~5-6s spacing avoided 429). Confirmed installed versions (readme Stable tag): wpforms-lite 2.0.1.1, flexible-shipping 6.12.1, wp-dark-mode 5.3.10, parcelpanel 4.6.0, goaffpro 2.7.12, triple-whale 1.0.3. Artifacts saved at /home/kali/workspace/animeape/plugin_versions.txt plus raw readmes /tmp/rd_ .txt. Two slugs resolved as NOT separately installed: (1) 'jetpack' — /wp-content/plugins/jetpack/readme.txt and all jetpack plugin files return 404; the observed jetpack/v4, wccom-site/v3 and wc-admin/plugins/connect-jetpack REST routes are the automattic/jetpack-connection library bundled inside WooCommerce, not a Jetpack plugin install, so 'jetpack' in f001 is a false positive and carries no separate CVE surface. (2) 'woosuite-restriction-rules' — readme.txt 404 (the f002 'readme 200' observation no longer reproduces); no woosuite namespace/asset is present, so this plugin is not confirmed installed. CVE cross-reference results: WPForms unauth chunked-upload RCE CVE-2026-10818 affects WPForms PRO <=1.10.1.1 (fixed 2.0.0) but only wpforms-lite 2.0.1.1 (patched, free) is installed and no 'wpforms'/'wpforms-pro' plugin dir exists; the three nopriv actions wpforms_upload_chunk_init / wpforms_upload_chunk / wpforms_upload_finalize all return '0' HTTP 400 on /wp-admin/admin-ajax.php, confirming the vulnerable handlers are absent. parcelpanel 4.6.0, flexible-shipping 6.12.1, goaffpro 2.7.12, triple-whale 1.0.3 and wp-dark-mode 5.3.10 have no published unauthenticated RCE/arbitrary-file-write CVE matching their installed versions (all prior CVEs are authenticated or affect older ranges; parcelpanel's only unauth issue is reflected XSS <=4.3.2). Conclusion: no confirmed-match unauthenticated RCE exists among these versions; this intent is exhausted and yields no new RCE path.",
      "properties": {
