      "info": "i006 explored to exhaustion — the elementor-one/v1 plugin-management lead is a confirmed DEAD END, no unauth plugin activation or code execution. Live re-verification: the full route set of /wp-json/elementor-one/v1 is unchanged (no new routes). f003's premise that the slug whitelist is validated BEFORE the auth check is a FALSE POSITIVE — it is standard WordPress REST ordering (enum/validate_callback runs during parameter parsing, then permission_callback always returns 401 for anonymous callers). Evidence: POST /plugins/{slug}/activate returns HTTP 401 code 'unauthorized' ('not allowed to manage plugins for this site') for ALL 8 whitelisted slugs (angie, elementor, elementor-pro, manage, site-mailer, image-optimization, pojo-accessibility, cookiez); invalid slug -> 400 rest_invalid_param. Other state-changing routes likewise gated: POST /plugins install -> 401 rest_cannot_install_plugin; GET /plugins -> 401 rest_cannot_view_plugins; POST /plugins/{slug}/upgrade -> 401 rest_cannot_manage_plugins; POST /connect/authorize, /connect/disconnect, /settings -> 401 rest_forbidden; themes -> 403. Bypass attempts failed: X-HTTP-Method-Override / ?_method= -> 404 rest_no_route; GET/PUT/PATCH/DELETE on activate -> 404. OPTIONS on activate leaks the slug whitelist with no auth, but POST-only. No OAuth/token secret leaked in homepage JS; elementor/v1/library/connect still token-gated. Net: no shell/command execution via this intent; it is exhausted. Details and full route inventory in /home/kali/workspace/animeape/i006_elementor_one.md.",
