      "concluded": "2026-09-25T02:18:58Z",
      "info": "i010 (read-based secret recovery) explored; NO wp-config.php creds or mcp_jwt_secret recovered. Confirmed incremental facts: (1) CVE-2024-9935 is the 'PDF Generator Addon for Elementor Page Builder <=1.7.5' path-traversal (rtw_pgaepb_dwnld_pdf via /elementor-84/?rtw_generate_pdf=true&rtw_pdf_file=...), NOT an Elementor-core LFI as the intent assumed; that plugin is NOT installed (its readme.txt and public class file both 404; the plugin-dir request returns the theme soft-404 homepage, size ~300KB), so this LFI is inapplicable. (2) Cloudflare WAF returns 403 'Attention Required!' for /wp-content/debug.log, /.env and /.git/config (literal patterns blocked at the edge), so wp-config backups/debug.log/.git are not directly reachable. (3) No JS source maps exist for installed assets (rey-core c-general.js.map, elementor frontend.min.js.map, woocommerce add-to-cart.min.js.map all 404); /wp-content/uploads/ and /wp-content/uploads/elementor/css/ are not listable (404 theme page). Homepage (752KB, saved /home/kali/workspace/animeape/home2.html) contains no inline api-key/secret/token/password values. (4) CONFIRMED readable-artifact vector: /wp-content/uploads/wpdesk-logs/wpdesk_debug.log returns HTTP 200 (1480 bytes) and is publicly readable; contents are low-value only — old wpdesk-sender debug lines (2022-03-15) and 2024-05-28 entries proving 'WooCommerce Flexible Shipping PRO' (flexible-shipping-pro/flexible-shipping-pro.php) was installed then deactivated; no credentials/tokens. The wpdesk-logs directory itself returns 200 with an empty body (no autoindex); /wp-content/uploads/wc-logs/, /logs/, /woocommerce-logs/ are 404. (5) No secret/DB-credential read primitive was found among installed components; this read-based dimension yields no path to forging the MCP JWT. Log-file exposure (wpdesk_debug.log) is the only confirmed unauth file-read on the target and is not sensitive. Artifact: /home/kali/workspace/animeape/home2.html.",
