      "concluded": "2026-09-25T04:27:52Z",
      "info": "i012 explored; a viable gadget source was located but command execution was NOT confirmed. Incremental facts: (1) Full active-plugin inventory (46 plugins) recovered from the /tmp/allopts.json 'active_plugins' entry — corrects earlier recon: the cache plugin is object-cache-pro/object-cache-pro.php (not 'objectcache'), woosuite-core + woosuite-restriction-rules, user-role-editor-pro, wp-rocket, wp-mail-smtp, wordpress-seo-premium, gtm-server-side, url-shortify-premium, pw-gift-cards, pw-bulk-edit, woocommerce-analytics, woocommerce-gateway-nmi/authorize-net-cim, reviewscouk-for-woocommerce, wc-fraud-blocker-main, alttext-ai, beprofit, imagify, wp-headers-and-footers, kiwisizing, japan-checkout-requirements, secure-copy-content-protection, woo-preview-emails are all installed. (2) POP gadget source found: Monolog 2.x (Logger::API=2) is bundled TWICE in installed plugins — wp-mail-smtp as WPMailSMTP\\Vendor\\Monolog\\... and flexible-shipping as FSVendor\\Monolog\\... — and its primitives match phpggc Monolog/RCE1: FSVendor\\Monolog\\Handler\\SyslogUdpHandler has protected $socket and close(){ $this->socket->close(); } and inherits Handler::__destruct()->close(); BufferHandler::close()->flush()->$this->handler->handleBatch($this->buffer)->handle()->processRecord() which iterates $this->processors calling $processor($record) (processors ['current','system'] yields system($cmd)). phpggc Monolog/RCE1 payload generated OK (phpggc cloned to /tmp/phpggc; generated O:32:\"Monolog\\Handler\\SyslogUdpHandler\"... with inner BufferHandler, socket/handler self-reference r:2). NOTE: Handler::__destruct wraps close() in try/catch(Throwable) so chain failures are silent; a local test unserializing the class-name-rewritten (FSVendor\\) payload against the real bundled Monolog classes produced NO command output, so execution is UNPROVEN. (3) Delivery-path constraint resolved: gsf's createUpdateOption applies getDataGSF()=addslashes() then str_replace('\\\\','',$option_value), stripping ALL backslashes, so namespaced class names cannot be delivered that way; the sibling createMultipleOptions path ($_REQUEST['options_value'] raw -> stripslashes() -> json_decode(...,true) -> per-key update_option) DOES preserve backslashes if the JSON text is sent with every backslash doubled (4 raw backslashes -> 1 literal; \\\\\" -> \"), so it is the viable delivery route for a namespaced serialized payload into wp_gsf_shop_secret. (4) Trigger is secret-independent: class-wp-gsf-rest-controller.php:22 calls getWpShopSecretKeyGSF() BEFORE the secret comparison, so ANY POST /wp-json/gsf/v1/update-options triggers the unserialize; admin-ajax.php?action=gsf_wp_action -> registerStoreGSF -> WP_GSF_HttpClient::callAPI also triggers it. (5) Additional gsf sinks reviewed and found non-RCE: addGoogleVerificationTokenGSF() is hooked on wp_head and does printf(get_option('wp_gsf_google_token_string')) (format-string only, ArgumentCountError on PHP 8); generalAdminNoticeGSF() echoes wp_gsf_admin_notice_content_html (XSS only); several add_action() hook NAMES are themselves read from writable wp_gsf_ options (wp_gsf_product_page_view/shop_page_view/cart_page_view/checkout_page_view/thankyou_page_view) but callbacks are fixed. (6) Live secret state unchanged from f008: a getShopData request with the original value returned 'shop secret Mismatch', confirming wp_gsf_shop_secret is still the leftover s:4:\"TEST\"; and still needs restoring to s:32:\"3a28e768873c7bfb28fa689a61000f89\"; via createUpdateOption. Local artifacts: /tmp/plugins/src (extracted plugin sources, incl. both Monolog copies), /tmp/phpggc, /tmp/test_monolog.php, /tmp/payload.bin, /tmp/payload_prefixed.txt. No shell/command execution was obtained.",
